; NextDAAD sprite animation fixture. STIMULUS fixture: tests\build-tests.ps1
; asserts the compiled bytes; tests\sprites_dump.py drives it over ZRCP and
; reads the DEBUG snapshot after every ANYKEY. Sets: 002 torch 8-bit,
; 003 32x32 one-shot, 006 4-bit two blocks, 015 8-bit in block 2, 017 4-bit
; 126 patterns (16810 bytes, two pool banks), 018 4-bit 2x2 composite with
; two blocks, 020-033 copies of 002 for the record ceiling and the cache
; ceiling. S11 stops all first: 017 needs every one of the 126 pattern
; half-slots the pointer does not hold. S12's four starts take the cache
; past its sixteen entries, so the last one evicts. S13 starts one more set
; with four still live, so the eviction is READABLE: the victim is the
; coldest entry no record names. S14 exercises the 4-bit relative path:
; neighbouring cells sit in different palette blocks and the two frames
; swap them.
;
; MOUSE 0 0 then MOUSE 0 1 centres and shows the pointer so the pointer mask
; and the pointer-over-4-bit check are live. SHOWMS alone never moves the
; sprite: only GETMS (MOUSE n 3) polls the Kempston mouse and repositions
; it, so the three silicon observation steps (S1, S2, S14) wait in the
; fontsw.dsf tracking-loop idiom (MOUSE 104 3 + INKEY + SKIP, then a PAUSE
; 25 debounce) instead of ANYKEY; flags 104-107 are free (100-103 feed
; GFX 100 20 at S7). Every other step keeps ANYKEY. PICTURE 1 needs a picture file: the -Sprites leg stages the
; palette card as 001.NX2, and S15 is the stop-all that PICTURE performs.
;
; ANYKEY, not PAUSE 0: it is the V2 wait-for-key condact and behaves the same
; whether or not -v3 is given, so the fixture does not depend on the header
; version. SYSMESS 16 carries a trailing #n so the next MESSAGE starts on its
; own line.

/CTL
_
/VOC
NORTH  2  noun
SOUTH  3  noun
LOOK   4  verb
/STX
/0  "It's too dark to see anything."
/1  "I can also see:"
/2  "What now?"
/3  "What next?"
/4  "What should I do now?"
/5  "What should I do next?"
/6  "I didn't understand."
/7  "I can't go in that direction."
/8  "I can't do that."
/9  "I have with me:"
/10 "I am wearing:"
/11 " "
/12 "Are you sure?"
/13 "Another go?"
/14 " "
/15 "OK."
/16 "Press any key.#n"
/17 " "
/18 " "
/19 " "
/20 " "
/21 " "
/22 " "
/23 "I'm not wearing one of those."
/24 "I can't. My hands are full."
/25 "I already have the _."
/26 "There isn't one of those here."
/27 "I can't carry any more things."
/28 "I don't have one of those."
/29 "I'm already wearing the _."
/30 "Y"
/31 "N"
/32 "More..."
/33 ">"
/34 " "
/35 " "
/36 "I now have the _."
/37 "I'm now wearing the _."
/38 "I've removed the _."
/39 "I've dropped the _."
/40 "I can't wear the _."
/41 "I can't remove the _."
/42 "I can't remove the _. My hands are full."
/43 "The _ weighs too much for me."
/44 "The _ is in the"
/45 "The _ isn't in the"
/46 ", "
/47 " and "
/48 ".#n"
/49 "I don't have the _."
/50 "I'm not wearing the _."
/51 "."
/52 "There isn't one of those in the"
/53 "Nothing."
/54 " "
/55 " "
/56 " "
/57 "I/O Error"
/58 " "
/59 "File name error."
/60 "Type in name of file."
/MTX
/0 "S1 GFX 2 19#n"
/1 "S2 GFX 6 19#n"
/2 "S3 GFX 15 19 refused: block 2 claimed#n"
/3 "S4 GFX 6 21#n"
/4 "S5 GFX 15 19 cache hit#n"
/5 "S6 GFX 255 21#n"
/6 "S7 GFX 100 20 set 3 at 40,100#n"
/7 "S8 GFX 253 20 refused#n"
/8 "S9 eight starts then a ninth#n"
/9 "S10 restart of a live set#n"
/10 " "                             ; retired slot: S11 moved to /11
/11 "S11 two-bank set#n"
/12 "S12 cache full, one eviction#n"
/13 "S13 set 33 evicts the coldest cached set#n"
/14 "S14 4-bit composite with relatives#n"
/15 "S15 PICTURE stops all#n"
/16 "S16 320-wide: composite (0,0), torch (200,100), pointer#n"
/OTX
/0 "a brass lamp"
/LTX
/0 ""
/1 "The sprite lab."
/CON
/0
NORTH 1
/1
SOUTH 0
/OBJ
/0    1   1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   _ _
/PRO 0
> _ _   MOUSE 0 0
        WINAT 4 40
        WINSIZE 24 40
        CLS
        MOUSE 0 1
        GFX 2 19
        MESSAGE 0

$poll1
> _ _   MOUSE 104 3
        INKEY
        SKIP $next1
> _ _   SKIP $poll1

$next1
> _ _   PAUSE 25
        GFX 6 19
        MESSAGE 1

$poll2
> _ _   MOUSE 104 3
        INKEY
        SKIP $next2
> _ _   SKIP $poll2

$next2
> _ _   PAUSE 25
        GFX 15 19
        MESSAGE 2
        ANYKEY
        GFX 6 21
        MESSAGE 3
        ANYKEY
        GFX 15 19
        MESSAGE 4
        ANYKEY
        GFX 255 21
        MESSAGE 5
        ANYKEY
        LET 100 3
        LET 101 40
        LET 102 0
        LET 103 100
        GFX 100 20
        MESSAGE 6
        ANYKEY
        GFX 253 20
        MESSAGE 7
        ANYKEY
        GFX 255 21
        GFX 20 19
        GFX 21 19
        GFX 22 19
        GFX 23 19
        GFX 24 19
        GFX 25 19
        GFX 26 19
        GFX 27 19
        GFX 28 19
        MESSAGE 8
        ANYKEY
        GFX 255 21
        GFX 2 19
        GFX 2 19
        MESSAGE 9
        ANYKEY
        GFX 255 21
        GFX 17 19
        MESSAGE 11
        ANYKEY
        GFX 255 21
        GFX 29 19
        GFX 30 19
        GFX 31 19
        GFX 32 19
        MESSAGE 12
        ANYKEY
        GFX 33 19
        MESSAGE 13
        ANYKEY
        GFX 255 21
        GFX 18 19
        MESSAGE 14

$poll3
> _ _   MOUSE 104 3
        INKEY
        SKIP $next3
> _ _   SKIP $poll3

$next3
> _ _   PAUSE 25
        PICTURE 1
        DISPLAY 0
        MESSAGE 15
        ANYKEY
        MOUSE 0 1
        GFX 18 19
        LET 100 2
        LET 101 200
        LET 102 0
        LET 103 100
        GFX 100 20
        MESSAGE 16

$poll4
> _ _   MOUSE 104 3
        INKEY
        SKIP $next4
> _ _   SKIP $poll4

$next4
> _ _   PAUSE 25
        END
/END
